//! The `scroll-snap-stop` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property defines
//! whether or not the scroll container is allowed to "pass over" possible snap positions.
//!
//! Initial: normal. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - always: The scroll container must not "pass over" a possible snap position; and must snap to
//! the first of this elements' snap positions.
//! - normal: When the visual `viewport` of this element's scroll container is scrolled, it may "pass
//! over" possible snap positions.
//!
//! Grammar: normal | always
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scroll-snap-1/#propdef-scroll-snap-stop
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/scroll-snap-stop
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

